BT /F1 10 Tf 72 718.4 Td (Nine groups took part, with between four and eleven members each. Six groups met weekly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 706.4 Td (and three met every other week. Sessions lasted between forty and ninety minutes. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 694.4 Td (total we observed seventy-two sessions and coded just over four thousand speaking turns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 682.4 Td (Two coders worked through a shared subset of twelve sessions to check agreement, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 670.4 Td (they matched on the paragraph being discussed in nearly nine out of ten turns. Where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 658.4 Td (they disagreed, the cause was usually a speaker who jumped between two nearby sections) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 646.4 Td (in a single remark.) Tj ET
